Subject: [PATCH] loot: a gathering node needs a free bag slot

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

infra#2813, and the freeze on infra#2800. `LootObject::IsLootPossible`
(src/Mgr/Item/LootObjectStack.cpp:280-348 at the pinned SHA) checks the
gameobject's flags, the bot's skill, the required skill value, and whether it
is carrying a mining pick or a skinning knife. It never once asks whether the
bot has anywhere to put what it is about to gather.

With zero free bag slots that makes the action NON-TERMINATING. `add all loot`
re-adds the node on the next tick, `IsLootPossible` says yes again, and inside
INTERACTION_DISTANCE - 2 (3.33 yards) `open loot` fires at relevance 8.0 and
preempts `new rpg do quest` at 3.0 forever. Engine.cpp:220 breaks on the first
successful action, so nothing below 8.0 ever gets a turn.

Measured on the live realm (infra#2800, verified against acore_world.gameobject
and characters):

    gameobject guid 206507, entry 1617 "Silverleaf"  (-9329.5, -801.2, 66.0)
    Grug                                             (-9328.2, -803.9, 66.017)
    distance 2.98 yards

Grug held that position to within 0.1 yard for 8 hours 31 minutes, across a
worldserver restart, with 40 of 40 bag slots used. The other four likewise. It
reads as a pathfinding bug or a questing bug and it is neither: he is not
walking anywhere, he is re-casting on a herb three yards away that he has
nowhere to put.

WHY THE FIX IS HERE AND NOT ON THE RELEVANCE NUMBERS

The obvious lever is the 8.0. infra#2800 investigated exactly that and DECLINED
it: `nc -loot` removes CORPSE looting too - AddAllLootAction::Execute iterates
nearest game objects AND nearest corpses (AddLootAction.cpp:25-38) - and 10 of
the family's 14 open quests are item-collection quests, including quest 60
"Kobold Candles", whose Large Candles drop off kobold corpses. The cheaper
`nc -gather` is provably inert, because herb nodes enter through `loot`'s own
`add all loot`, which has no skill filter at all.

So the relevance side is untouchable, and this is the other half of the
product: an action at 8.0 only starves everything below it because it never
terminates. Make it terminate and the contest resolves itself, with no priority
changed anywhere.

WHY IT IS SCOPED TO GATHERING NODES AND NOT TO ALL LOOT

The guard sits BELOW the `skillId == SKILL_NONE` early return, so corpses and
ordinary chests are not affected. That is deliberate, and it is the whole
reason this check is exact rather than a heuristic:

  * A CORPSE can hold MONEY, and money needs no bag slot. A bot with full bags
    should still walk over and take the copper, and it still can.
  * A GATHERING NODE yields items only - there is no money in a herb. With no
    free slot there is nothing it can produce that the bot can accept, so
    refusing it is not a policy, it is arithmetic.

WHAT IT DELIBERATELY GETS WRONG, STATED PLAINLY

At exactly zero free slots a bot will also refuse a node whose herb would have
STACKED onto a partial stack it already carries. `IsLootPossible` runs before
the object is opened, so the loot contents are not knowable at this seam and a
precise test is not available here. The error is in the safe direction - a
refusal to loot can never destroy or lose anything - and it only bites at zero,
which is a state nothing should be sitting in for eight and a half hours
anyway. The alternative, which is checking nothing, is what this patch exists
to fix.

`GetFreeInventorySpace` is the core's own count of the backpack plus every
equipped bag (PlayerStorage.cpp:470-490). Counting it here by hand would be a
second and worse copy of it.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Any free-slot or CanStoreNewItem check landing in `IsLootPossible` upstream, or
upstream gaining a general "do not queue loot the bot cannot accept" filter in
AddAllLootAction. No upstream PR is open for this yet.

APPLIES TO

    mod-playerbots @ 60e6555e4e4b552ee4c6551b466aff648916f38b
    src/Mgr/Item/LootObjectStack.cpp, LootObject::IsLootPossible

    This uses NO new upstream member. `Player::GetFreeInventorySpace()` is
    public in the pinned core fork (Player.h:1269 at
    47960183bb03b83e8943eb2f0f39c16df9710c9d) and `bot` is already a complete
    `Player*` everywhere else in this function, which calls `bot->HasItemCount`
    and `bot->GetSkillValue` a few lines further down.

diff --git a/src/Mgr/Item/LootObjectStack.cpp b/src/Mgr/Item/LootObjectStack.cpp
index 6911b5c..90376e8 100644
--- a/src/Mgr/Item/LootObjectStack.cpp
+++ b/src/Mgr/Item/LootObjectStack.cpp
@@ -315,12 +315,30 @@ bool LootObject::IsLootPossible(Player* bot)
     if (go && go->HasFlag(GAMEOBJECT_FLAGS, GO_FLAG_INTERACT_COND) && !go->ActivateToQuest(bot))
         return false;
 
+    // BELOW THIS LINE IS GATHERING ONLY. A corpse or a plain chest returns
+    // here, and it must: a corpse can hold MONEY, which needs no bag slot,
+    // so a bot with full bags should still walk over and take the copper.
     if (skillId == SKILL_NONE)
         return true;
 
     if (skillId == SKILL_FISHING)
         return false;
 
+    // infra#2813 / infra#2800: a gathering node yields ITEMS ONLY, so with
+    // no free bag slot there is nothing it can produce that the bot can
+    // accept. Without this the loot never completes, `add all loot` re-adds
+    // the node every tick, and `open loot` at relevance 8.0 preempts
+    // `new rpg do quest` at 3.0 forever - measured as one character
+    // motionless within 2.98 yards of a Silverleaf node for 8h31m with
+    // 40/40 bag slots used.
+    //
+    // At exactly zero this also refuses a node whose herb would have
+    // stacked onto a partial stack already carried; the loot contents are
+    // not knowable before the object is opened, and erring toward refusing
+    // to loot can never lose anything.
+    if (bot->GetFreeInventorySpace() == 0)
+        return false;
+
     if (!botAI->HasSkill((SkillType)skillId))
         return false;
 
